It is evening now.
I put my phone on the table.
In Mexico it is exactly midday right now.
I call my family.
Everyone is on the screen: my parents, my sister Sofia and my brother Diego.
Even our dog Lola is there!
"Happy birthday!" they shout together and sing for me.
I laugh and thank them.
"How was your week?" I ask.
"Did you have a lot of stress?"
"No, the week was very quiet," my father answers.
"Sofia, what are you doing right now?" I ask my sister.
"I am studying for university," she says.
"And how are you, Diego?" I ask my brother.
"Everything is great, I already had a football game today," he explains.
Then I see Lola on the sofa.
"Is Lola actually still stealing shoes?" I ask, laughing.
"Oh yes," my mother sighs, "only yesterday she had Dad's shoe in her mouth again."
We talk for quite a while longer.
It is nice just to hear from home.
